# Line-ending policy. Shell scripts and Dockerfiles run inside Linux containers,
# so they MUST be LF — a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true) would otherwise
# ship CRLF, and a `#!/bin/sh\r` shebang makes the kernel exec `/bin/sh\r`
# -> "exec ...: no such file or directory" at container start.
*.sh        text eol=lf
Dockerfile* text eol=lf

# Binary fixtures must never be line-ending-normalized.
*.pptx      binary

# --- sandbox/ (the golden template + pre-baked base image; built on the Windows VM) ---------
# The image is BUILT+DEPLOYED from a Windows VM (ADR-0015 / D9). A Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true would otherwise ship CRLF into shell scripts / Dockerfile / Caddyfile and
# break the container at start (`#!/bin/sh\r` → "no such file or directory"). Force LF across the
# whole tree; lockfiles are text; images/fonts are binary so they are never normalized.
sandbox/**              text eol=lf
sandbox/**/*.png        binary
sandbox/**/*.jpg        binary
sandbox/**/*.jpeg       binary
sandbox/**/*.gif        binary
sandbox/**/*.webp       binary
sandbox/**/*.ico        binary
sandbox/**/*.woff       binary
sandbox/**/*.woff2      binary
sandbox/**/*.ttf        binary
sandbox/**/*.otf        binary
